","user":{"login":"kisg","id":406832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNjgzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/406832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg","html_url":"https://github.com/kisg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-09T20:11:06Z","updated_at":"2025-02-09T20:11:06Z","body":"This bug is on PowerVR GPUs with the GLES backend. The other issue was with the Vulkan backend on Adreno GPUs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646565629/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2963848041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102413#issuecomment-2963848041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102413","id":2963848041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wqLtp","user":{"login":"kisg","id":406832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNjgzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/406832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg","html_url":"https://github.com/kisg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T18:54:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T18:54:05Z","body":"For those who are stumbling on the same issue, the workaround is to use ANGLE over Vulkan, because we cannot control when updated GL drivers will be released for these devices (and when the individual users will upgrade to the new releases).\n\nCheck here for more insights of the various issues of these GL drivers: https://forums.imgtec.com/t/bxm-8-256-long-list-of-driver-issues/3891","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2963848041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2964494252","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102413#issuecomment-2964494252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102413","id":2964494252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wspes","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T22:58:37Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T23:06:02Z","body":"@kisg  Have you tried it out yourself yet?\n\nI'm not sure if this information is helpful yet. (It's primarily about WebGL 2.0 / Chromium.)\n\n-----------\n\nEDIT:  https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/android?msg=BPDqxi468PLrp2oJv\n> All this is currently implemented in LibGodot for the embedded display server (not yet in the public branch, but \"soon\"), but could be used in other display servers as well.\n\nThat sounds good!\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2964494252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2965327365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102413#issuecomment-2965327365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102413","id":2965327365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wv04F","user":{"login":"kisg","id":406832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNjgzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/406832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg","html_url":"https://github.com/kisg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-12T06:46:39Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T06:46:39Z","body":"@Alex2782 Thanks for your question. Probably I should have been more clear. I only linked the IMG forum thread to show that the exact same driver version has not only problems with Godot, but also with Chromium (or more specifically running another game engine in Chromium using WebGL). According to the IMG developers there are newer versions of their GL driver, which fixes some issues reported there, but they can't control when that driver version gets into vendor builds, and when users will be able to start using them.\n\nSo yes, as I wrote on the forum, we tested the ANGLE fallback and have a more advanced implementation that can detect problematic drivers at runtime and fall back to ANGLE when required.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2965327365/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5083043453","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102413#issuecomment-5083043453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102413","id":5083043453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLvkWfQ","user":{"login":"DiplomaticRobot","id":40128966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTI4OTY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40128966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot","html_url":"https://github.com/DiplomaticRobot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DiplomaticRobot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T10:14:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T10:14:47Z","body":"Still reproducible on 4.6.2-stable. We are seeing this same crash in a production mobile game (Compatibility renderer, arm64) on MediaTek mt6855-family devices with PowerVR GPUs, on Android 14 and 15.\n\nAffected devices so far:\n- Motorola Moto G54 5G (cancunf) — same device as the OP\n- Motorola Moto G56 5G (bogota)\n- POCO (citrine)\n- CUBOT X100\n\nThe SIGSEGV is inside the vendor shader compiler (`libufwriter.so`, `GLSLCompileToUniflex`) during a runtime `glCompileShader` call issued from `GodotRenderer.onDrawFrame`. Note this does not involve `Skeleton3D` in our case — it appears to trigger on shader compilation in general, so the issue may be broader than the current title suggests.\n\nRepresentative backtrace (app paths redacted):\n\n```\n#00 pc ...  /vendor/lib64/mt6855/libufwriter.so\n...\n#08 pc ...  /vendor/lib64/mt6855/libufwriter.so (GLSLCompileToUniflex+15972)\n#09 pc ...  /vendor/lib64/egl/mt6855/libGLESv2_mtk.so\n#11 pc ...  /vendor/lib64/egl/mt6855/libGLESv2_mtk.so (glCompileShader+116)\n#12-#24     libgodot_android.so\n#25 pc ...  libgodot_android.so (Java_org_godotengine_godot_GodotLib_step+484)\n#28         org.godotengine.godot.gl.GodotRenderer.onDrawFrame\n#30-#32     org.godotengine.godot.gl.GLSurfaceView$GLThread.run\n```\n\nFor reference, Filament hit what looks like the same PowerVR compiler crash and worked around it in their shader generation: google/filament#5118 (fixed by google/filament#7051 — the PowerVR compiler crashed when `gl_Position` was written twice in a vertex shader). Possibly a similar authoring-pattern workaround is feasible in Godot's GLES3 shader generation.\n\nHappy to provide full traces or test builds on the affected devices if useful.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5083043453/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]